@NODE iNTRODUCTiON "iNTRODUCTiON OF ACCESS-SPY V1.1"

Ever seen all those local lamers coming to your board, scanning the file-dir
leeching ALL files since they last were in and finally logging off?
Ever wished to allow that people logging in only at a specific time?
Or even lower their daily Downloadlimit for a specific-time?

OK, here it is: Access-Spy lets you specify, when certain users are allowed
to enter your board and when NOT! You can even change their Downloadlimit,
access-level and so on ONLY for a specific time-range! On all other times
they just have their normal stats! Sounds great, eh?

So u`re able to prevent the BBS from being busy at the main-time, when all the
new releases are spread! Forget your sorrows about missing the hottest warez,
only coz a lamer leeched 5MB of old stuff at exactly that time!
Just give all Elite-Traders a higher access-level at that time, and that`s it!

And don`t forget to use the other @{"Features" LiNK FEATURES} of ACCESS-SPY.

@ENDNODE

@NODE FEATURES "FEATURES OF ACCESS-SPY V1.1"


         JUST HAVE A LOOK AT THE COOL FEATURES OF ACCESS-SPY V1.1:
         =========================================================


         - written in "pure" C (Hi to all ASM-Coders out there :^)

         - fully configurable with the included Cfg-File

         - `SPECIAL VERSIONS` available directly from the author or
           from any oSiRiS-Member-Board! Just call, and u got one!!

         - gives the users their correct settings back, even after
           a BBS-CRASH (just be sure to recover the files in the
           Users-Dir! Then all works perfect!)

         - Access-Spy detects, if a new user gets a previous empty
           slot - the user-datas won`t interfere

         - only shows a message to the user, if he calls in the
           time-range, the restrictions take place!
           at all other times nobody will recognize the door
           (I call that `silent-mode` hehe)

         - you can set restrictions for ALL USERS

         - you can set restrictions for GROUP-MEMBERS or users with
           a special Conference-Access

         - you can set restrictions for SPECIFIC USERS
           (you hate ONE person on your board? Just use ACCESS-SPY)


    AND NOW I GUESS I GAVE YOU ENOUGH REASONS TO @{"INSTALL" LiNK iNSTALLATiON} ACCESS-SPY V1.1

@ENDNODE

@NODE iNSTALLATiON "iNSTALLATiON OF ACCESS-SPY V1.1"

iNSTALLATiON TO @{"AMi EXPRESS V2.xx" LiNK AMiEXPRESSV2.xx}.

iNSTALLATiON TO @{"AMi EXPRESS V3.xx" LiNK AMiEXPRESSV3.xx}.

@ENDNODE

@NODE AMiEXPRESSV2.xx "iNSTALLATiON TO AMi EXPRESS V2.xx"

TO iNSTALL THE DOOR LOAD UP THE CUSTOMCOMMANDS (/X V2.2x OR BELOW) OR
BBS.CMD (/X V2.3x) AND ADD THE FOLLOWiNG LiNE TO THE LiST.


          11 SPACES iN         
          |
--------------------------------------------------          
*access   XM10DOORS:ACCESS-SPY/ACCESS-SPY
--------------------------------------------------
||        ||| |           
||        ||| ` 'DOORS:ACCESS-SPY/ACCESS-SPY' iS THE LOCATiON OF
||        |||    THE FiLE.
||        |||
||        ||` 10 THE MiNiMUM ACCESS TO USE THiS DOOR. CHANGE iT TO WHAT
||        ||     YOU GUESS iS ACCEPTABLE FOR YOUR BOARD.
||        ||
||        |` 'M' FOR A MULTiNODE BBS ('S' FOR A SiNGLE NODE BBS).
||        |
||        ` 'X' FOR A XIM - DOOR.
||
|`COMMAND TO START THE DOOR.
|
`-RETARD OPTiON. TO MAKE SURE THEY ONLY USE 'access' & ONLY  'access'
  TO GET THE DOOR TO COME UP. iF NOT USED, THiNGS SUCH AS 'accessme' AND
  'access%$§%$§&' WOULD STiLL BRiNG UP THE DOOR.


  USE THE LiNE BETWEEN THE LiNES ONLY. THE OTHER PARTS ARE JUST AN
  EXPLANATiON TO MAKE SURE YOU KNOW WHAT EACH PART iS DOiNG (SiNCE
  NOONE WOULD TELL ME BACK iN THE DAYS WHERE i DiDN'T KNOW WHAT WAS
  GOiNG ON!)  

  NOW COPY THE DiRECTORY 'ACCESS-SPY' FROM THE LHA-ARCHiVE INTO THE DOORS:
  -DIR OF YOUR BBS.

  BE SURE TO COPY ALSO THE USERS-SUBDiRECTORY INSIDE THE ACCESS-SPY-DIR!!
  iT`S iMPORTANT COZ THE USERS CORRECT BBS-DATAS WILL BE STORED iNTO iT!

  THEN JUST EDIT THE FILE(S) `BBS:Node[x]/login.txt[.gr]` as follows:

~
~CC_access
... rest of previous login.txt

  REMEMBER TO DO SO FOR EVERY (!) NODE YOU`VE GOT!


  AT LAST EDiT THE @{"CONFiGFiLE" LiNK CONFiGFiLES}. YOU`LL FiND iT iN 'DOORS:ACCESS-SPY/',
  NAMED AS `ACCESS.CFG`.

@ENDNODE

@NODE AMiEXPRESSV3.xx "iNSTALLATiON TO AMi EXPRESS V3.xx"


THE FiRST THiNG TO DO iS TO COPY THE FiLES FROM THE LHA-ARCHiVE TO YOUR BBS.
BE SURE TO CORRECTLY CREATE THE DIR `DOORS:ACCESS-SPY/` AND(!) iT`S SUBDiR
`USERS/`.

THE ICON `ACCESS.iNFO` HAS TO BE PLACED iNTO `BBS:COMMANDS/`.
JUST ADJUST THE TOOLTYPE `ACCESS=10` TO THE MiNiMUM-VALUE OF THE ACCESS-LEVEL
A USER MUST HAVE TO START THE DOOR!


THEN JUST EDIT THE FILE(S) `BBS:Node[x]/login.txt[.gr]` as follows:

~
~CC_access
... rest of previous login.txt

REMEMBER TO DO SO FOR EVERY (!) NODE YOU`VE GOT!


FiNALLY EDiT THE @{"CONFiGFiLE" LiNK CONFiGFiLES}. YOU`LL FiND iT iN 'DOORS:ACCESS-SPY/ACCESS-SPY',
NAMED AS `ACCESS.CFG`.

@ENDNODE

@NODE CONFiGFiLES "HOW TO EDiT THE CONFiGFiLE `ACCESS.CFG`"

=====================[Example Config-file]===========================

-[ALL USERS]---------------------------------------------------------
BEGINKICKTIME=07:00
ENDKICKTIME=07:30
KICKFILE=doors:access-spy/Kick.txt
BEGINRATIO=18:00
ENDRATIO=01:30
RATIO=3
BEGINBYTELIMIT=18:00
ENDBYTELIMIT=01:30
BYTELIMIT=2000000
-[CONF-ACCESS]-------------------------------------------------------
-[EliteUser]---------------------------------------------------------
BEGINRATIO=18:00
ENDRATIO=01:30
RATIO=0
BEGINBYTELIMIT=18:00
ENDBYTELIMIT=01:30
BYTELIMIT=15000000
-[NormalU]-----------------------------------------------------------
BEGINRATIO=08:00
ENDRATIO=11:30
RATIO=0
-[SINGLE USERS]------------------------------------------------------
-[SPiDeR]-----------------------------------------------------------------
BEGINKICKTIME=18:00
ENDKICKTIME=00:00
KICKFILE=doors:access-spy/kickno5.txt
BEGINACCESS=08:30
ENDACCESS=15:30
ACCESS=200
-[MuMu]----------------------------------------------------------------
BEGINKICKTIME=23:30
ENDKICKTIME=23:50
BEGINRATIO=15:00
ENDRATIO=15:30
RATIO=5
-[END OF USERS]------------------------------------------------------

==========================[  cut here again   ]======================

What does that mean?

-[ALL USERS]------- that just indicates the beginning of a section, in which
                    the restrictions affect ALL USERS

BEGINKICKTIME=07:00 thats the beginning of the time-range, in which the user
                    gets kicked out of the board immediately after logging in
                    it`s usefull, if you need some time every day, to do
                    internal things such as netcalls

ENDKICKTIME=07:30   its the end of the above mentioned time-range

KICKFILE=doors:a... here you can insert path and filename of a text-file that
                    will be shown to the user before he gets kicked off

BEGINRATIO=18:00    thats the beginning of the time-range, in which the user
                    gets his ratio changed to the value mentioned later

ENDRATIO=01:30      thats the end-time of the ratio-time-range

RATIO=3             thats the value the user`s ratio gets changed to!!
                    it doesn`t matter, which value the user had earlier, so
                    a user with disabled gets 3:1-Ratio here AND a user with
                    1:1 also gets 3:1
                    if you want to avoid, that a user gets a BETTER ratio
                    than before, just enter his new ratio into the single-user
                    section (see below)

BEGINBYTELIMIT=18:0 thats the beginning of the time-range, in which the user
                    gets changed his daily Download-Limit

ENDBYTELIMIT=01:30  hmmmmmmmmmm, guess what? :^)

BYTELIMIT=2000000   value of the new downloadlimit (in Bytes)

BEGINACCESS=08:30   thats the beginning of the time-range, in which the user
                    gets changed his Access-Level  (be carefull with that!!)

ENDACCESS=15:30     the end of that time-range

ACCESS=200          the new access-level    (handle it carefull, otherwise it
                    could happen that every New-User has an access of 200 hehe)
                    i suggest you use that option ONLY in the Single-User-Sect.
                    so u always know, whose access-level gets changed!!
                    that`s usefull, if you wanna give your cosys a level of
                    255 for that time, when u are at work, so he can handle
                    the sysop-job for you!

-[CONF-ACCESS]----- that indicates the beginning of a section, in which the
                    restrictions only affect users with the specified conf-axx
                    (great for GROUP-MEMBERS or COSYSOPS!)

-[EliteUser]------- that indicates the beginning of the restrictions-section
                    for all users, that have conf-access 'EliteUser'
                    all restrictions inside this area only affect users with
                    that conf-acces, all others are NOT affected
                    thats great for example for group-members, coz they all
                    have the same conf-axx and you only need to specify ONCE,
                    what different restrictions ALL the group-members get at
                    certain times! (ever thought of giving the group-members a
                    dizzy only from 06:00am to 05:00pm? hehehe)
                    In the example above, I give all Elite-Users a disabled
                    at the same time, all other users got only 3:1-ratio!
                    So you cann assure, that your active users got a better
                    ratio than the local lamers!

-[SINGLE USERS]---- that indicates the beginning of a section, in which the
                    restrictions only affect CERTAIN users

-[SPiDeR]---------- this indicates the beginning of the restrictions-section
                    for user `SPiDeR` !!
                    just write down such a section for every specific user u
                    want to change different access-things ..... for example
                    you could give your cosys` always 10MB downloadlimit, even
                    if ALL other users got only 1MB at that time!!!

-[MuMu]------------ the same for user `MuMu` !
                    (just to be sure you got it right hehehheh)

-[END OF USERS]---- that shows the end of the user-section
                    very important line, don`t remove it!


                     ==============================
                      iMPORTANT THiNGS TO MENTiON:
                     ==============================

All entries in a section override the SAME entries in the section before, if
the user is affected from both sections!
That means, that all entries in the Single-Users-Section override the SAME
entries in the Conf-Access-Section AND in the ALL-Users-Section, i.e. in the
above example, the Elite-Users always have a disabled ratio from 18:00 (6 pm)
till 01:30 (am), coz the entry in the Conf-Access-Section OVERRIDES the entry
in the All-Users-Section!

By that, you could for example give ALL group-members a downloadlimit of let`s
say 5 MB, and only your Cosys gets more if you specify him by his slot-number
in the Single-Users-Section!

Another thing is, you can show a specific user a different kick-text-file,
for example a little information you want ONLY HIM to know! All other users
will get the kick-text-file specified in the All-Users-Section.

If you handle that in the right way, u`ve got an extremely powerfull tool
without having to write a config-file for EVERY lame User!


You can mix up the lines between two `-[   ]------` as you like, i.e. the order
of the Keyword-Lines (BEGINKICKTIME,etc) is not fixed.

But NEVER CHANGE the order of the `-[  ]---`-lines! Anything you mix up with
that lines leads to a door-crash!!!!

On the other hand, u can always delete a section, u don`t need! For example,
if you only wanna use Access-Spy for ALL USERS, u can simply delete the SINGLE
USERS-Section and the CONF-ACCESS-Section!
If u wanna handle later on specific users then just add the SINGLE USERS-
Section again!

@ENDNODE       

@NODE WayOfWork "THAT`S THE WAY ACCESS-SPY WORKS"


AccessSpy just looks into the cfg-file on a user-logon, and the user will be
confronted with 2 possible actions:


(i)  Nothing.
     That just happens, if the user calls within his regular time-range or if
     the slot-no wasn`t found in the cfg-file and no All-Users-restrictions
     were made.
     The user won`t notice anything about the start of Access-Spy!


(ii) If the users slot-number was found or if he calls in a time-range
     specified in the config-file, he will be told about the restrictions
     he has for that call OR (if he calls in the kick-time) a text-file will
     be shown to him, and after that he is immediately logged out!


@ENDNODE       

